  "flavor": {
    "name_bank_key": "khraaldurn",
    "phonemic_palette": "Khraaldurn (Durnkad frost-dialect): the shared hard-frame/soft-vowel/short-syllable Durnkad, with the frost-dialect drift - root vowels DRAW OUT and round (-un -> -uun, a -> aa, o -> oo) and final stops soften a touch, a slow, cold, rolling weight. The common-word stock is the shared Durnkad (one tongue); the lengthening shows in speech and in the marked forms (titles, deities, the realm's own name).",
